Expected elements: present

Every must-show renders: nav with resolver, breadcrumb, full hash, `Succeeded`, the neutral `Not observable` badge, a seven-row Overview whose first row is the sole provenance marker (`Real Aztec mainnet data`), four sections each stating a permanent absence, a footer with all three marks drawn. No debug/retry/spinner, no trace reference, no error tone.

Change (a) landed: `SELECTOR` and `RAW` both render `—`. Change (b) landed as copy but regressed as layout — `COST · TRANSACTION FEE` now wraps to three lines in a 163px label column, making that row 89px against 38px for the five above it, with 50px of dead space under a one-line value. The label column has 294px of slack beside it.

Change (c) is my P1, and it is not a density complaint. The new sentence scopes both refusals to "blocks 67651–67686". This transaction is at `67650:0` — stated twice on the same page — so by the page's own arithmetic it is neither inside the replay window nor "below block 67650", while the card above says the runtime refused *it*. The reader is left unable to place the transaction in front of them.

Density: the DATA row is 263px of a 540px grid, 49%, still ahead of every fact and still carrying chain-level telemetry. The page is 2909px — 2.7 screens — and 63% of a 1920px viewport is canvas.

Fixes: scope the refusal sentence to the capture window that produced it; widen the label column.

Rating: 4/10

